From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: handle the HTT PPDU ID format indication

WLAN.HK 2.8 and later firmware sends HTT_T2H_PPDU_ID_FMT_IND (0x30, HTT
3.106) once per radio at bring-up: for each field it packs into a PPDU ID
(HW scheduler command id, ring, sequence index, link, command type, TQM
command, MAC id, CRC), whether it is present, its width and its bit
offset. ath11k only ever compares PPDU IDs, so it needs none of this, but
the unknown type ends in "htt event 48 not handled" at warning level on
every boot. Name the type and dump the message at HTT debug level.

Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -1191,6 +1191,7 @@ enum htt_t2h_msg_type {
 	HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_PPDU_STATS_IND = 0x1d,
 	HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_EXT_STATS_CONF = 0x1c,
 	HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_BKPRESSURE_EVENT_IND = 0x24,
+	HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_PPDU_ID_FMT_IND = 0x30,
 };
 
 #define HTT_TARGET_VERSION_MAJOR 3
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -2258,6 +2258,11 @@ void ath11k_dp_htt_htc_t2h_msg_handler(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 	case HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_BKPRESSURE_EVENT_IND:
 		ath11k_htt_backpressure_event_handler(ab, skb);
 		break;
+	case HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_PPDU_ID_FMT_IND:
+		/* The bit layout of the firmware's PPDU IDs; ath11k only compares them. */
+		ath11k_dbg_dump(ab, ATH11K_DBG_DP_HTT, NULL, "htt ppdu id format: ",
+				skb->data, skb->len);
+		break;
 	default:
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "htt event %d not handled\n", type);
 		break;
